	(descr "JST PH series connector, S6B-PH-K (http://www.jst-mfg.com/product/pdf/eng/ePH.pdf), generated with kicad-footprint-generator. Extracted verbatim (pads, graphics, 3D model reference) from the footprint embedded as J_CAM0 in the original hand-drawn FoveaCamDuo-PCB.kicad_pcb (KiCad 9, git 289fb6c); not in the stock KiCad 10 library. Original library id: Connector_JST:JST_PH_S6B-PH-K_1x06_P2.00mm_Horizontal_NoSilkScreen. Drill 2026-10-07 (owner, v0.1.2): 0.80 mm finished (0.75 before): JST ePH.pdf p1 gives the PCB hole as 0.7 +0.1/0 and note 3 asks for a larger hole on glass-fibre boards; at fab tolerance a 0.75 hole can finish at 0.67 (JLCPCB -0.08) or 0.623 (Advanced PCB -0.127), below JST's 0.7. Pads stay 1.2 x 1.75 mm: plated ring 0.20 mm (>= JLCPCB 0.18, Advanced 0.178).")
